1pcx|v|To have ( a notion or idea) come into the mind again, as previously perceived, known, or felt; to have a renewed apprehension of; to bring to mind again; to think of again; to recollect; as, I remember the fact; he remembers the events of his childhood; I cannot remember dates. ; To be capable of recalling when required; to keep in mind; to be continually aware or thoughtful of; to preserve fresh in the memory; to attend to; to think of with gratitude, affection, respect, or any other emotion. ; To put in mind; to remind; -- also used reflexively and impersonally. ; To mention. ; To recall to the mind of another, as in the friendly messages, remember me to him, he wishes to be remembered to you, etc. ; To execise or have the power of memory; as, some remember better than others.	d:26jv,99,6;2cj,14,3;1431,13,3~26jv,99,6;2cj,14,3;1431,13,3	D:fuq,53,4~fuq,53,4
